<div class="modal fade" id="modal-help" tabindex="-1" aria-labelledby="help-title" aria-hidden="true">
  <div class="modal-dialog modal-lg modal-dialog-centered modal-dialog-scrollable">
    <div class="modal-content">
      <div class="modal-header"><h2 class="modal-title" id="help-title">What makes this durable?</h2><button type="button" class="btn-close" data-bs-dismiss="modal" aria-label="Close"></button></div>
      <div class="modal-body">
        <ol class="help-steps">
          <li><strong>Pick a device and start a session.</strong> The session is a database and a working directory on that device.</li>
          <li><strong>Send work, then close this tab.</strong> The agent keeps running on the device. Open the page again and it shows where the run is.</li>
          <li><strong>Change App State, then fork.</strong> Forks keep their own conversation but share the device's App State.</li>
          <li><strong>Interrupt on purpose.</strong> Esc stops foreground work. Background jobs keep running until you stop them.</li>
          <li><strong>Try the limits.</strong> Turn on Read only, or the command guard, and ask the agent to delete something.</li>
          <li><strong>Restart the device mid-tool.</strong> The run resumes from its checkpoint. A tool that may have half-run comes back as interrupted instead of running twice.</li>
        </ol>
        <div class="alert alert-info mb-0">Durable means checkpointed, not exactly-once. A message is admitted once, but an outside effect (a payment, a deploy) may have happened just before a crash. Effects still need their own idempotency.</div>
      </div>
      <div class="modal-footer"><button type="button" class="btn btn-outline-secondary" data-bs-dismiss="modal">Close</button></div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>

